[White "2.4 Protected Passed Pawns"]
[Black "Example 82- Danielsson- R. vs. Larsson- J.- Swedish Team Championship 2007"]
[Result "*"]
[FEN "8/8/5p2/4p3/4P1pp/5PkP/6P1/5K2 w - - 0 1"]

 { A protected passed pawn can also play the role of securing a draw. Here Black has just played ...g5-g4, making a last attempt at squeezing a point out of a drawish pawn ending. How would you react? } 1. { -KEY- } fxg4 $1 ( { The game went } 1. hxg4 $2 h3 $1 2. gxh3 Kxf3 $1 { (obstruction) } 3. Ke1 Kg3 4. Ke2 Kxh3 5. Kf3 Kh4 6. g5 fxg5 $1 { and White resigned. } ) 
Kf4 2. Kf2 Kxe4 { Now Black enjoys a protected passed pawn on e5, but White is just in time to create his own one on the h-file. } 3. g3 $1 hxg3+ 4. Kxg3 Kd3 5. Kf2 $1 ( { Not } 5. h4 $2 e4 { and Black queens with check. } ) 
e4 6. Ke1 Ke3 7. h4 $1 Kf4 8. h5 Kg5 9. Ke2 { Draw. } f5 
